  "generation": [
    {
      "id": "citizen-pass1",
      "prompt": "Create a cleaner native-pixel-art variant of the tiny medieval town resident in this enlarged source reference. Deliver ONE sprite on genuine transparent background. The output is intended for an exact16x16 canvas with the standing human only10 logical pixels tall, head at roughly row4 and soles at row13. Keep its warm restrained brown/tan palette and simple elevated game view. Make the head, tan tunic, two arms, dark belt and separated brown legs/feet read as a coherent ordinary citizen at that tiny size. Adult balanced proportions, a small3x3 head, not a huge chibi head. A few face marks are optional; prioritize anatomy and posture. Use broad solid square pixel clusters, at most10 opaque colors, no antialiasing, no texture/noise, no accessories, no ground shadow or checkerboard. Keep ample transparent margins and the feet centered on x8. Treat the reference as palette/scale/style guidance; improve the current merged body shapes without making the character taller than10 native cells.",
      "output": "citizen/draft.png",
      "references": [
        "citizen/reference.png"
      ],
      "referenceEvidence": "Reference list retained in original generation record."
    },
    {
      "id": "tree-pass1",
      "prompt": "Edit this nearest-neighbor enlarged native24x32 tree sprite into one polished compatible game tree variant. Preserve the same canvas framing, contact position and overall size: a leafy olive-green broadleaf tree with a short warm brown trunk, seen from the existing elevated isometric game view. Keep source proportions and top-left light. Improve the canopy into a few readable overlapping leaf masses with coherent connected highlights and recessed shadows, and a visible fork connecting canopy to trunk. The trunk must not look like an orange rectangular stump. Use the same subdued olive, moss, dark-green and brown family, at most15 opaque colors. EXACT logical24x32 lattice, one solid color per square pixel, no subpixel detailing, gradients, smooth painting, scattered dots, extra black outline, glow or ground shadow. Single complete tree, true transparent background, leaves and trunk inside the source frame and same foot alignment.",
      "output": "tree/draft.png",
      "references": [
        "tree/reference.png"
      ],
      "referenceEvidence": "Reference list retained in original generation record."
    },
    {
      "id": "house-pass1",
      "prompt": "Edit this native32x40 medieval isometric house sprite into a clearer compatible architectural variant, preserving its exact frame, footprint, orientation, contact position and geometry. Keep the small warm plaster house, terracotta pitched tile roof and stone chimney. Ground and roof/eave axes must remain2:1 isometric, pillars and window jambs vertical. Keep the present mature building scale and roof volume; no enlargement, courtyard slab, enclosure, people or extra props. Improve readable door recess and simple framed windows on the visible walls, restrained roof tile rows and coherent plaster/wood/stone material clusters. Important: NO black or dark silhouette outline and NO dark pixel ring. Edge colors are the lit/shaded materials themselves. Use restrained connected native pixel shading, max32 flat colors, no antialiasing, fine painted texture, random speckles or grid. Every logical pixel is one square on the32x40 lattice. Real alpha transparency. Preserve roof/chimney headroom and the source ground-plane alignment.",
      "output": "house/draft-first.png",
      "references": [
        "house/reference.png"
      ],
      "referenceEvidence": "Reference list retained in original generation record."
    },
    {
      "id": "house-pass2",
      "prompt": "Image1 is the EDIT TARGET: the generated small isometric plaster house with terracotta roof. Image2 is the original game asset and STRICT ORIENTATION/ENTRY reference. Fix exactly one layout error: the front door in image1 is on the WRONG visible wall. Move the full-height door to the RIGHT-HAND wall, in the position occupied by the window in image1. The original in image2 clearly has its doorway on this RIGHT visible wall. Replace the old left-wall doorway with a modest framed WINDOW, leaving plaster below it. Do not rotate, mirror, recolor or reshape the building; keep roof ridge, chimney, posts, roof overhang, foundation outline, lighting and camera unchanged. Preserve vertical door/window jambs and2:1 isometric floor/eave directions. Keep the right-wall entry bottom on the original ground line and unobstructed. Target is native32x40 pixel art enlarged: use broad connected flat square color clusters at that logical scale, not tiny subpixels, gradients, texture or random dots. No black/dark silhouette outline or added border. Keep the entire source frame and real alpha transparency, no ground platform, text, extra props or checkerboard. Only one corrected house.",
      "output": "house/draft.png",
      "references": [
        "house/draft-first.png",
        "house/reference.png"
      ],
      "referenceEvidence": "Two references identified by the exact prompt; refs array was absent from the retained generation record."
    }
  ],
